<title>USA: Teva's Acyclovir gets tentative FDA OK.</title>
<headline>Teva's Acyclovir gets tentative FDA OK.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Teva Pharmaceutical Industries Ltd said Monday it has received tentative U.S. Food and Drug Administration approval to manufacture and market Acyclovir capsuls.</p>
<p>The company said Acyclovir is the generic equivalent of Glaxo Wellcome Plc's Zovirax, an antiviral product.</p>
<p>The patent on Zovirax expires April 22, Teva said, adding the drug has annual U.S. sales of about $140 million.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610.))</p>
</text>
